From 7027ad86a7ea2e27a6c0e54a97e4aab1930a546f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:48:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 18/36] B70-QSA-Q02: B70_QSA_TOPK=native_det, native top-k with
 the torch selector's output

Exact 0.0 indexer scores tie often at the top-k boundary, and the native
SYCL top-k has no specified tie order, so native and torch can attend
different blocks for the same scores. native_det runs native, puts every row
in the torch order (descending score, lower column first) and recomputes on
the torch path only the rows whose k-th score is tied. Under graph capture
(decode) it is the torch path, which needs no host sync. Opt-in; default
unchanged. The native call moves to _qsa_topk_native so tests can stub it.
